msgid "Mixing security tests"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If it becomes necessary to test security features using both `@TestSecurity` "
"and Basic Auth (which is the fallback auth\n"
"mechanism when none is defined), then Basic Auth needs to be enabled "
"explicitly,\n"
"for example by setting `quarkus.http.auth.basic=true` or `%test.quarkus.http."
"auth.basic=true`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Similarly, if it becomes necessary to test security features using both "
"`@TestSecurity` and Bearer token authentication,\n"
"you can leverage both like in the example below:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Bearer token authentication mechanism is used, because a Bearer access token "
"is sent with the HTTP request."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"No authorization header is present, therefore the Test Security Extension "
"creates user `Bob`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Path-based authentication"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@TestSecurity` can also be used when xref:security-authentication-"
